[
    "Model evals test the LLM itself, including its general capabilities and failure modes.",
    "Model evals evaluate the model as a component.",
    "App evals test an LLM-powered system end-to-end.",
    "Examples of app eval systems include a RAG chatbot, a retriever plus LLM pipeline, and a JSON-output scoring tool.",
    "The whole system, components, dataset, runtime setup, and tooling are part of an app eval.",
    "Model evals aim to judge the model's capabilities and risks.",
    "Model evals ask whether the model can do a task and whether it has dangerous capabilities.",
    "Model evals aim to understand model strengths and weaknesses independent of a particular product.",
    "App evals decide product readiness and whether the system is good enough to ship or put into production.",
    "App evals ask whether prompt V2 improved over V1, whether RAG answers are grounded, whether the agent completes tasks correctly, whether the chatbot is safe for users, and whether latency is acceptable.",
    "Model eval metrics are capability-focused and safety-focused.",
    "Model eval criteria include task performance, general competence, and dangerous-capability checks.",
    "App eval metrics include task correctness and quality.",
    "App eval quality criteria include correct answers, clear and simple explanations, and groundedness in the user's content.",
    "App evals also include safety and tone criteria.",
    "App eval operational metrics include P95 latency, cost per query or token usage, model cost comparisons, reliability and availability, monitoring and observability, and drift or regression tracking.",
    "Both model evals and app evals are part of the full LLM-eval testing setup.",
    "The full LLM-eval testing setup includes the target, criteria, and method.",
    "Methods used for both include human judgment, automated checks, LLM-as-judge, and production feedback.",
    "Tests should be systematic and repeatable.",
    "Datasets should be used so versions can be compared.",
    "The terms model eval and application eval were introduced to simplify the topic.",
    "The terms model eval and application eval are not formal industry-only terms."
] 

