    "Ordering / attention bias: the generator tends to rely more on higher-ranked, earlier documents.",
    "If the correct fact is lower in the K results, the model can ignore it and choose a conflicting fact from an earlier document.",
    "Prompt/system-prompt bias: the system prompt can instruct the generator to prioritize certain documents or weigh context in a particular order.",
    "The generator may prefer wrong facts because of prompt/system-prompt bias.",
    "Fact blending / context mixing: the model can merge facts from multiple documents and produce a composite but incorrect answer.",
    "It may take "Python = 6 weeks" from one document and apply it to "ML".",
    "Model probabilism / non-determinism: LLMs are probabilistic.",
    "Even with the same context, they may produce different outputs and sometimes invent details.",
    "Insufficient grounding constraints: if the generator is not explicitly constrained to only use retrieved context, it can fall back to internal knowledge or invent details.",
    "Output-format/expectation mismatch: if you expect a specific format or specificity and the model is not guided well, it can output a different and wrong form of the answer.",
    "Lack of re-ranking / poor context ordering: without re-ranking or a way to surface the most relevant document first, correct evidence can be present but low-priority and effectively ignored.",
    "Ambiguous or underspecified user query: if the question is vague, the generator may fill gaps with plausible but incorrect facts.",
    "These are the typical causes when retrieval is correct but the generator still hallucinates."
] 

