[
    "The recommendation is to use non-blocking, durable, queryable logging with late-signal attachment and PII handling.",
    "At runtime, a small structured event should be emitted immediately so the chat response path is not blocked.",
    "The emitter should hand events to a background worker or async queue that writes to a durable store.",
    "The background writer should batch, retry, and write append-only records so writes never block the main flow.",
    "Late signals such as escalations, post-conversation emails, and support tickets should be ingested later as events and linked by conversation_id and turn_id.",
    "Append-only structured events are recommended for replayability and durability.",
    "Events should be indexed by conversation_id, session_id, user_id, and timestamp for fast querying.",
    "Captured signals and computed metrics should be stored as separate fields or downstream materialized columns.",
    "All artifacts used in the response should be versioned so experiments and rollbacks are possible.",
    "PII should be masked before it is written into the durable store.",
    "Raw PII should only be kept in a tightly controlled vault if absolutely needed.",
    "A recommended schema is one JSON event per turn with minimal write overhead in the critical path.",
    "The top-level required fields include project_id, conversation_id, session_id, user_id, turn_id, parent_turn_id, timestamp_utc, and role.",
    "User and assistant text fields include user_text, assistant_text, prompt_template_id, prompt_template_version, and optionally prompt_text.",
